  {
    "__EMPTY": "Description of sheet"
  },
  {
    "__EMPTY": "See how risks are categorised across both taxonomies. The Causal Taxonomy of AI Risks, adapted from Yampolskiy (2016), classifies risks by its causal factors (1) entity (human, AI), (2) intentionality (intentional, unintentional), and (3) timing (pre-deployment, post-deployment). The Domain Taxonomy of AI Risks adapted from Weidinger (2021) classifies risks into 7 AI risk domains: (1) Discrimination & Toxicity, (2) Privacy & Security, (3) Misinformation, (4) Malicious Actors & Misuse, (5) Human-Computer Interaction, (6) Socioeconomic & Environmental, and (7) AI System Safety, Failures, & Limitations."
  },
  {
    "__EMPTY": "How to use"
  },
  {
    "__EMPTY": "This sheet shows the percentage of risks which relate to each of our causal factors (e.g., entity, intention and timing), and how these overlap with domains. For instance, the extent to which the risk 'Exposure to toxic content' was presented as i) Human or AI caused, ii) intentional or unintentional, or iii) occuring pre- or post-deployment. You can see specific risks catagorisation by filtering our AI risk database. For more see detail please see our report."
  },
